//! check: fail(E0201)
//! phase: lex
//! conforms: gram.lex.newline, gram.fmt.brace
//!
//! s252 (wolf-lang#822, yew's fuzz fork): a multi-line `if` condition
//! with its `{` at the start of the next line, C's shape, is E0201 by
//! design. The line ending in `3` takes a terminator
//! (`[gram.lex.newline]`: a literal ends the statement), a `{` that
//! begins a line begins a block statement of its own, and the
//! formatter keeps the brace on the construct's line
//! (`[gram.fmt.brace]`). The refusal says so and offers the edit that
//! joins the lines (`b > 3 {`); the multi-line condition itself is
//! legal, broken after its operator (`a > 2 &&`). lupin 0.1.54 refuses
//! it at E0201 too.

fn main() {
    let a = 3
    let b = 4
    if a > 2 &&
        b > 3
    {
        print("both")
    }
}
